A||N||5||banditbalz||Transmission Failure?  Do I need to drop engine?||||1||
Z||000000||banditbalz||05-06-2001||09:33 PM||||Tonight while driving a friend noticed oil spraying out of my car, I stopped to notice that oil was coming from my tranny and the car refuses to go into neutral, Any ideas what MAY be wrong?  do I need a new tranny? (4spd) and does the engine need to be dropped for this procedure.<P>Your responses are appriciated!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||05-06-2001||11:06 PM||||Ouch, sounds like a split tranny case. It you are lucky, you've blown a seal, but if not, you'll need a new tranny.<P>A moment of silence...<P><BR>Amen.||||reg||9
Z||000002||theogre||05-06-2001||11:07 PM||||First you need to find out why it puked it's oil. That will tell you allot it will.||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||05-07-2001||04:18 PM||||I was with bandit when it happened (my CAA/AAA got him back to the FieroShop for repairs)  still awaiting word on it, damn thing.  <P>Does it help that when you push the clutch inthe car DOES move but makes a grinding sound?||||reg||1
Z||000004||grinthock||05-07-2001||06:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>Ouch, sounds like a split tranny case. It you are lucky, you've blown a seal, but if not, you'll need a new tranny.<P>A moment of silence...<P><BR>Amen.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>A moment of silence indeed!  TIS a cracked casing.....  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||PBJ||05-07-2001||07:45 PM||||No, you don't have to drop the engine.  You will have to support the engine from the top and unbolt the back of the cradle,and swing the cradle down and forward on frt bolts.  That is after you remove the exhaust off the Y pipe and unbolt mounts from cradle.  I separated the ball joints and pulled axles out of trans-leaving them in the hubs, up on the car.||||reg||1
